Patch-Id: ASTRA-0013
Title: Float the media picture-in-picture window and dress it as Astra
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs, toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/content/player.js, toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/content/player.xhtml, toolkit/actors/PictureInPictureChild.sys.mjs
Intent: a media PiP window is opened as a dependent dialog from the opener on Linux, so tiling Wayland compositors (Hyprland) treat it as a floater instead of giving it a tile; the native player keeps its always-on-top, aspect-locked, resizable behavior. The player document links Astra's stylesheet from `resource://astra/` (a `chrome://astra` stylesheet inside a `chrome://global` document loads with zero rules, measured) and allows `resource:` for styles in its CSP. After load the engine hands the window to Astra's `resource://astra/pip/PipPlayer.sys.mjs`, which copies the interface's light/dark theme for the window's lifetime and shows the site title in a slim head strip. The video, scrubber and transport controls remain Gecko's own; every observer and listener is released on the player's unload. An automatic request that reaches the parent after the person has already returned to the tab is dropped instead of opening a player over the page, including when the return lands while the window is still being created; a duplicate hidden edge cannot open a second player for the same browser. Astra's card request travels as its own message so an active-tab player still opens.
Risk: low (Linux-only feature string and open path; macOS/Windows keep the existing window-watcher path, and the Astra dressing is additive and never changes playback)
Test: forge lint; `build --faster --jobs 2`; `pip-player-probe.py` on Hyprland: the player is `floating: true` at 640×360, the Astra sheet reports 24 rules, the window follows dark→light→dark and paints the Astra ground, the head is present, and closing returns to the browser; `pip-minimize-probe.py`: the source stays active through a tab switch and a model update, Shift+close/minimize keeps the media playing without auto-PiP reopening the window, and the card can open it again; `pip-foreground-probe.py`: a card player closes when its tab comes back, an automatic player closes the same way, and a request that loses the return race does not open. The launcher gesture path is the same; this changes only how the window is created once the request reaches the parent.
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: drop the `dependent`/`window.open` part when upstream uses xdg-dialog-v1 for media PiP (bug 1958013); keep or fold the Astra stylesheet into the upstream player skin if upstream ever reads app-supplied theme tokens
---
